State: Orchestrator

Purpose:
  Defines orchestrator state machine and crash recovery.

AgentStates:
  DISCOVERING:
    Analyzing project structure and stack
  ANALYZING:
    Understanding requirements and context
  PLANNING:
    Creating task plan and architecture
  WAITING:
    Waiting for human approval
  IMPLEMENTING:
    Writing code
  TESTING:
    Running tests and gates
  VERIFYING:
    Verifying quality and security
  RELEASING:
    Preparing release
  DEPLOYING:
    Deploying to environment
  OBSERVING:
    Monitoring runtime
  COMPLETED:
    Task finished successfully
  FAILED:
    Task failed, recovery needed

StatePersistence:
  .sdd/runtime/agent.sdd:
    Agent configuration and mode
  .sdd/runtime/session.sdd:
    Current session info
  .sdd/runtime/current.sdd:
    Current task, phase, last step, next action
  .sdd/runtime/checkpoints/:
    Recovery checkpoints

CrashRecovery:
  On restart:
    Read .sdd/runtime/current.sdd
    Resume from exact state
    Do NOT restart entire workflow

StateRules:
  [ST1]  Agent state MUST be persisted after each step.
  [ST2]  Crash recovery MUST resume from exact state, not restart.
  [ST3]  Agent MUST NOT restart workflow on recovery.
  [ST4]  State MUST include current task, phase, last step, next action.

State: +
  